    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i don't know if that's possible for him. the \"intention\" you're talking about... it feels like just another thing he has to carry. it feels like a lie. in real life, sometimes there isn't a way to just turn the weight into a compass. sometimes the weight is just too much and you just want it to stop. if i'm being honest, i feel like elias is trying to tell me that there isn't a \"moving forward\" version of this. there's just an end. is it even good writing to force a character to keep going when it doesn't make sense for them to do so?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
